Problem Statement:
We want to increase the amount of plastic that is recycled in the Fayetteville high school area. We will separate the plastic and dispose of it properly. This is important due to the high contents of plastic that is sent to the land fill instead of being properly recycled. 
Stakeholders/ Users:
Jeffrey O’Connell who will need to see out progress and design
Engineering class: who will maintain and operate the center
Teachers who will recycle
Principles who may be willing to provide support and resources
Custodial staff will be able to use this to more efficiently dispose of plastic
Students who will be using our design
Project Goal: 
Reduce the amount of sitting plastic waste within the area of Fayetteville high school. As well as convert it into 3d printer filament. To get as many people to recycle using our center as possible.
Design criteria:
Using the free blueprints gained from the Precious Plastic website.
Being able to be operated and maintained by a class of high schoolers. 
Need a proper sorting system
Be affordable to manufacture by high schoolers
Constraints:
Money
Resources
Time
What type of plastics are accepted
Initial measures of success:
Research has gone well and have now transferred into groups to start compiling information for the start of the project.
Major unanswered questions:
How much time will we have to do this project, our overall budget, materials we will have access to, where we will put it.



